I've left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and the body can't use `http-client` without a world import that the graph definition doesn't grant. Adding that import here would widen the node's authority. The fetch also has a data problem: `RunInfo` has no text field, so `<the input's text>` has nothing to bind to. If the grant is extended in the graph definition, and the input gains a field to query on, the enrichment can be added then. Until then, the node below reads only the subscriptions state.

I assumed the store key is `urls`, with one URL per line, and an absent key yields an empty list, so `present(urls)` holds.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

